; The dead double. Winning 42 p. 65 (S-0090-b, S-0091-b), p. 95 (S-0126-c);
; played in Hands 28, 30, 34 and 35 (S-0131-d, S-0131-e, S-0136-f, S-0137-c,
; S-0146-d, S-0148-d, S-0150-c, S-0151-a, S-0151-g); declined in Hand 34
; (S-0147-a). In Hand 28 trick 6 both the left setter's doubles are dead, and
; the book says either may go (S-0131-d).
; Rule, in our words: a double wins only a trick led in its suit, and only a
; tile whose higher end is that suit leads it. Once no live tile outside your
; hand can lead its suit, the double is dead: throw it first on a trick you
; cannot follow (the 0-0 is dead in any hand but its holder's; the 1-1 once the
; 1-0 is gone, the 3-3 once the 3-0, 3-1 and 3-2 are). A throw is a tile given
; to a trick you do not take: in every one of the book's throws the thrower can
; take nothing, so the rule does not fire where a tile of his would take the
; trick (a ruff). The book throws no count double: the 5-5 is a ten, and where
; it goes is the count rules' business. The bidder on lead with a
; setter's trump still out cashes a dead double at once: it wins only when he
; leads it, and he may not have the lead again (Hand 27 trick 3).
; The cash is for a bidder who cannot draw: in Hand 27 he will lose the lead
; again because trumps are out that he cannot pull (S-0126-c). Holding the
; highest trump still out, out of crisis, he draws first (bidders-plan.silas,
; the book's guideline 1, S-0038-b), and the cash waits (2026-10-14, #146;
; before, it fired ahead of the draw).
; New: no gate has it. In an 84 it is the defender's watch list run dry
; (S-0090-b): a double is kept while some live tile outside the hand could be
; the bidder's off in its suit, and dropped when none can.
; GAP likelihood: in Hand 34 trick 2 the partner throws the 6-2 before his dead
; 1-1, keeping low fours as a decoy for an opponent's reading (S-0147-a); the
; rule throws the 1-1 there, which the book throws at trick 4 (S-0148-d).

(include book)

(policy dead-double
  (rule throw-a-dead-double (play dd)
    (viewer me)
    (discard dd)
    (dead-double dd)
    (count dd 0)
    (not (can-take-it)))
  (rule cash-a-dead-double (play dd)
    (viewer b)
    (bidder b)
    (on-lead b)
    (not (no-setter-trump))
    (or (crisis) (none (roles t) (own-legal t) (boss-trump t)))
    (own-legal dd)
    (dead-double dd)))
